cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Babel Context Integrity"
message: "If you use this software or the handoff contract, please cite it."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Henry
    given-names: Scott
  - family-names: Colasante
    given-names: Anthony
abstract: >-
  A deterministic, offline verifier and machine-readable contract for agent
  handoff artifacts. Babel checks whether the structured record one agent hands
  to the next still satisfies a declared contract: whether commitments
  recompute, whether provenance reaches its authority root, whether constraints
  marked as surviving actually survived, and whether independently computed
  encodings agree. It deliberately separates structural integrity, semantic
  equivalence under tested fixtures, provenance, authority agreement, and
  external truth, and never collapses them into a single verdict.
keywords:
  - AI agents
  - agent handoff
  - context integrity
  - provenance
  - verification
  - continuous integration
license: Apache-2.0
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-08-11"
repository-code: "https://github.com/babel-context-integrity/babel-context-integrity"
